<P> kMoria has a lot more possible actions than iRogue or iLarn.
Currently, each hardware button's list of possible actions is the
same.  I would like to support binding for a larger set of actions,
but you may have noticed when you are setting the bindings that the
list already barely fits on the screen.  So, maybe I can give each
hardware button a different list... e.g. if no one binds "calculator"
to "north", leave "north" out of its list, and put in "change font" or
whatever else that people would find more useful than "north".  How
can I find out whether no one binds "calculator" to "north", and what
bindings people want to keep?  That is your job - answer this survey
and then I will know.

<P> This survey looks basically just like your Hardware Buttons form
in kMoria, except that the n/s/e/w are mashed together, and there are
a couple of new choices.  Let me know what bindings you use now, or
what bindings you would use in your ideal world.

